736	- adaptive model-committee weighting, automatic patch application, GitHub mutation, and direct cloud-provider APIs.
737	
738	Stop rule:
739	
740	> A new abstraction may be added to Phase 1 only when it is required to complete the single-user GitHub dogfooding loop, enforce an accepted hard invariant, or avoid a known irreversible schema contradiction. Otherwise it must be documented as a Phase 2, Phase 3, or post-MVP concern and must not block Phase 1 implementation.
741	
742	After `UBU-D0175`, new MVP blockers are allowed only when discovered during implementation of a concrete Phase 1 slice and accompanied by a blocker certificate naming the blocked object or file, failed acceptance criterion, unsafe fallback, minimum answer needed, and persistence impact. Phase 1 readiness is judged slice-by-slice rather than by global philosophical completion of the model.
743	
744	The minimum dogfooding loop that proves UbU’s core model is:
745	
746	1. bootstrap the operator, project context, available work window, constraints, and current or stale affect Snapshot;
747	2. import or load a curated UbU GitHub fixture with issues, PR/review/CI signals, milestone context, and source links;
748	3. map those inputs into Objectives, Tasks, External Events, Logs, UniverseState facts, and External References;
749	4. generate a Calendar with a default Plan for the next work window;
750	5. present one recommended next Task with an explanation of Objective value, dependencies, deadlines, affect constraints, worker status, and risk findings;
751	6. record completion, failure, snooze, rejection, decomposition, or override as Log evidence and trigger recalculation when appropriate;
752	7. preview or perform a human-approved UbU-managed GitHub projection update;
753	8. show a reconciliation or risk summary that makes the changed model inspectable.
754	
755	### 4.1.1 Phase 1 public demo criteria
756	
757	The Phase 1 public demo should use real UbU GitHub issues or a frozen fixture captured from real UbU GitHub data when live access is unsafe, unavailable, or non-reproducible.
